3 Steps to Implement the Hybrid System
Keep Your Core Nouns (Traditional)
Maintain your standard master data categories (e.g., Customers, Products, Locations). Give them unique, permanent identifiers (URIs or UUIDs).
Reify Your Relationships (Process)
"Reification" means turning a relationship into an object. Instead of a simple link like User-likes-Product, create a Interaction class. This class holds the time, intensity, context, and evolution of that "liking" process.
Materialize State Views
Use event streams to update the traditional ontology. The process stream runs continuously in the background. When a system needs a traditional, static answer (e.g., "What is the current stock count?"), the system reads the latest snapshot generated by the event history.





