To read the traditional static structure alongside its latest process state, use a SPARQL query that filters for the most recent transition activity:
sparql
PREFIX ex: <http://example.org>
PREFIX xsd: <http://w3.org>

SELECT ?doc ?feature ?partial ?currentState ?lastUpdated
WHERE {
  # 1. Fetch the traditional static ontology relations
  ?doc a ex:Document ;
       ex:hasFeature ?feature .
  ?feature a ex:Feature ;
           ex:hasPartial ?partial .
  
  # 2. Fetch the process activities linked to the feature
  ?transition ex:target ?feature ;
              ex:toState ?currentState ;
              ex:timestamp ?lastUpdated .
  
  # 3. Process Philosophy Filter: Keep only the latest event in time
  NOT EXISTS {
    ?otherTransition ex:target ?feature ;
                     ex:timestamp ?otherTimestamp .
    FILTER(?otherTimestamp > ?lastUpdated)
  }
}
